  "holistic_F_N": 3,
  "holistic_F_H": -3,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict mandatory reporting of all incidents including suspected, with 24h serious and 5-business-day other deadlines. S2 sets a 6.5% 55°C failure limit (above the 5% benchmark), provides results to customers/regulators but prohibits public per-model rates, and relies on corrective action. S3 requires new-unit shut-off by 24 months and 72-month retrofit; S4 requires built-in suppression from 36 months; S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with regulator-approved remedy flexibility and prompt notices."
